# ModDB Release Archive Structure

When creating a release archive for `hodvisualizer`, the zip must be ModDB-compatible.

## Required archive layout

- `modinfo.json` must exist at the **root** of the `.zip`.
- `HodVisualizer.dll`, `HodVisualizer.deps.json`, and `assets/...` must be at root-level paths (not nested under `hodvisualizer/`).
- Entry paths must use `/` separators (`assets/hodvisualizer/...`), never `\`. Vintage Story on Linux does not treat `\` as a separator, so assets and lang files fail to load.

## Packaging rule

- Build the archive with `.\scripts\package-release.ps1` (output: `release/hodvisualizer_<version>.zip`).
- Do **not** use `Compress-Archive` or Explorer "Send to > Compressed folder": they can write `\` separators.
- Do **not** zip the parent folder (`hodvisualizer/`) itself.

## Mandatory verification before handing archive to user

The script fails if `modinfo.json` is not at the root or any entry contains `\`. To re-check an existing archive:

`Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem; $z=[System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::OpenRead("<zipPath>"); $z.Entries | ForEach-Object { $_.FullName }; $z.Dispose()`

## Stop condition

If `modinfo.json` is not in archive root or any entry contains `\`, rebuild archive before reporting success.
